<figure class="ltx_figure" id="S7.F9" lang="en"><img alt="Refer to caption" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_portrait" height="798" id="S7.F9.g1" src="figures/grid.png" width="479"/>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 9</span>: </span><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Example results generated by Heptapod-H.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<div class="ltx_para" id="p3">
<span class="ltx_ERROR undefined" lang="en">\beginappendix</span>
</div>
<section class="ltx_section" id="S8" lang="en">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section">
<span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">8 </span>Model Configuration</h2>
<div class="ltx_para" id="S8.p1">
<p class="ltx_p">Table <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2510.06673v1#S8.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ 8 Model Configuration ‣ Heptapod: Language Modeling on Visual Signals"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> summarizes the three model scales for causal Transformer (Base, Large, Huge) used throughout our experiments. For continuous tokenizer, following MAR <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2510.06673v1#bib.bib25" title="">25</a>]</cite>, we configure the diffusion-style denoising MLP head with {6, 8, 12} blocks and widths {1024, 1280, 1536} for the Base, Large, and Huge models, respectively.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_para" id="S8.p2">
<p class="ltx_p">Table <a class="ltx_ref" href="https://arxiv.org/html/2510.06673v1#S8.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 8 Model Configuration ‣ Heptapod: Language Modeling on Visual Signals"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> investigates how to allocate depth between the causal Transformer and the 2D prediction head for Heptapod-L. A balanced split (16/16) achieves the best FID and IS. Shifting layers from the head to the backbone (24/8) degrades performance, and an extreme allocation (31/1) leads to a sharp drop in both FID and IS. These results indicate that the prediction head must retain sufficient depth to project the 1D causal context into 2D spatial distributions and to model position-wise interactions at scale.</p>
</div>
<figure class="ltx_table" id="S8.T3">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Model Configuration for causal Transformer.</span></figcaption>
<table class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr class="ltx_tr">
<th class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t"></th>
<th class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Base</span></th>
<th class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t"><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Large</span></th>
